      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 16",
      "hints": [
        "Use the number with the opposite sign."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3.3.03",
      "n": 3,
      "prompt": "Write the inverse of $1+\\sqrt{2}$ as $c + d\\sqrt{2}$ with rational $c$, $d$. Type $c$, then $d$.",
      "answer": {
        "type": "numbers",
        "values": [
          -1,
          1
        ],
        "ordered": true
      },
      "answerText": "−1 + √2",
      "solution": [
        "The inverse is 1/(1 + √2).",
        "Multiply the top and the bottom by √2 − 1. The bottom is 2 − 1 = 1.",
        "The result is √2 − 1 = −1 + √2."
      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 6–9",
      "hints": [
        "Rationalise the denominator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3.3.04",
      "n": 4,
      "prompt": "Write $(1+2\\sqrt{3})(2-\\sqrt{3})$ as $c + d\\sqrt{3}$. Type $c$, then $d$.",
      "answer": {
        "type": "numbers",
        "values": [
          -4,
          3
        ],
        "ordered": true
      },
      "answerText": "−4 + 3√3",
      "solution": [
        "Expand: 2 − √3 + 4√3 − 2 · 3.",
        "= 2 + 3√3 − 6 = −4 + 3√3."
      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 10–11",
      "hints": [
        "Expand the product. Use $(\\sqrt{3})^2 = 3$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3.3.05",
      "n": 5,
      "prompt": "Rationalise the numerator of $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x+2h}-\\sqrt{x}}{h}$.",
      "answer": {
        "type": "expression",
        "value": "2/(sqrt(x+2*h)+sqrt(x))",
        "variables": [
          "x",
          "h"
        ]
      },
      "answerText": "2/(√(x + 2h) + √x)",
      "solution": [
        "Multiply the top and the bottom by √(x + 2h) + √x.",
        "The top becomes (x + 2h) − x = 2h. The h cancels."
      ],
      "langType": "§2 ex. 12",
      "hints": [
        "Use $(a-b)(a+b)$ on the top."
      ]
    },
